      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "First, choose Ace and Zeppo for the starting lineup. Then, we need to choose 3 more players from the remaining 10 players. Since the order of the players in the lineup doesn't matter, we need to account for the permutations of the 3 players as well.\n\nThe formula for permutations is nPr = n! / (n-r)!, where n is the total number of items and r is the number of items to choose.\n\nFor 3 players, n = 10 and r = 3.\n\nnPr = 10P3 = 10! / (10-3)! = 10! / 7! = (10*9*8) = 720\n\nFor 5 players, we will have Ace, Zeppo, and 3 other players. Since we are choosing these 3 players from the remaining 10 players, the number of combinations is 10C3.\n\n10C3 = 10! / (3! * (10-3)!) = 10*9*8 / (3*2) = 720\n\nNow we multiply the permutations for Ace and Zeppo by the combinations for the remaining players:\n\n720 (peaks for Ace and Zeppo) * 8 (since there are 10C3 options for the remaining players) = 8640\n\nSo, there are 8640 different starting lineups possible for the Grunters.",
