      "text": "To solve this problem, we can use combinations. Since Ace and Zeppo are definitely in the starting lineup, we only need to choose 3 more players from the remaining 10 players.\nThe number of ways to choose 3 players from 10 can be calculated using the formula for combinations:\n   \\[C(n, k) = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\\]\nwhere \\(n\\) is the total number of players, \\(k\\) is the number of players to choose, and \"!\" denotes the factorial of a number.\n   \\[C(10, 3) = \\frac{10!}{3!(10-3)!} = \\frac{10!}{3!7!} = \\frac{10\\times9\\times8}{3\\times2\\times1} = 120\\]\nTherefore, there are 120 different starting lineups possible.",
